{"title":"Career roadmap · Bioinformatics Research Associate","role":"Bioinformatics Research Associate","summary":"A Bioinformatics Research Associate applies computational methods, statistics and biological knowledge to analyse biological data such as DNA/RNA sequences, genomes, transcriptomes, proteins, variants, molecular interactions and biological networks.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Bioinformatics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Biology","Computer Science","Statistics","Data Science"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a directly relevant career for a B.Sc. Bioinformatics graduate, although many advanced research positions increasingly prefer an M.Sc./M.Tech./PhD or strong research experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical research workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Biological Question","Experimental Data","Quality Control","Computational Analysis","Statistical Analysis","Biological Interpretation","Validation","Publication"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Sc. Bioinformatics"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Research Associate"},{"type":"flow","items":["Bioinformatics","Computational Biology","Life-Science Research"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct/near-direct for junior research roles"},{"type":"note","label":"Advanced research","text":"PG degree strongly improves progression"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Research Assistant, Junior Research Fellow, Bioinformatics Analyst, Bioinformatics Research Assistant, Research Associate, Computational Biology Analyst"},{"type":"note","label":"Assumption","text":"three/four-year B.Sc. structure depending on t